@@ -0,0 +1,23 @@
+# SMS sign-in integration
+
+This repository serves static files. The homepage includes the phone/code UI and WebOTP integration, but sending SMS and creating authenticated sessions require the following same-origin backend endpoints. Without them, the form displays a recoverable service error; it never accepts a code locally or simulates a successful sign-in.
+
+## Endpoints
+
+- `POST /api/auth/sms/request`: JSON `{ "phone": "+15551234567", "purpose": "rewards" }` (`purpose` may also be `order`). Return JSON `{ "challengeId": "opaque-server-challenge" }` only after scheduling delivery. A resend creates a new challenge and invalidates the previous code.
+- `POST /api/auth/sms/verify`: JSON `{ "challengeId": "opaque-server-challenge", "code": "012345", "purpose": "rewards" }`. Validate the challenge on the server, consume it once, set a secure HttpOnly SameSite session cookie, and return `{ "verified": true }`. The client then navigates to `/rewards` or `/order-online`.
+- Return HTTP 400/401/410 for incorrect or expired codes and 429 for rate limits. Other errors get a generic retry message. Return JSON and `Cache-Control: no-store`. For native form submissions without JavaScript, accept form-urlencoded data and return an accessible server-rendered code form or redirect after verification.
+
+Generate six-digit codes securely on the server; preserve leading zeros, expire codes promptly, enforce attempt limits and delivery throttles, and bind each opaque challenge to its phone number and sign-in session. Protect POST endpoints by checking the request Origin and enforcing same-origin CSRF protection. Never return the code to JavaScript, log codes, or treat client validation or cooldowns as security controls.
+
+## SMS delivery
+
+Serve over HTTPS. Replace `your-production-host.example` below with the actual page hostname (no scheme, port, or path). The origin binding must be the final line, with one space between tokens and no trailing signature:
+
+```text
+Your Daily Grind sign-in code is 012345. Do not share this code.
+
+@your-production-host.example #012345
+```
+
+WebOTP is feature-detected and listens before SMS delivery is requested. Pending listeners are aborted on submit, resend, number changes, failure, page exit, or after two minutes. Browsers without WebOTP retain `autocomplete="one-time-code"` and manual/paste entry in one labeled numeric-keyboard text input.
